<% content_for :title, "AWSM Security" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "public-site" %>
<%= render "shared/public_header" %>
<main class="site-container trust-page">
  <header class="trust-page__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Trust boundaries in plain language</p>
    <h1>The server coordinates. The client holds the keys.</h1>
    <p>AWSM separates Account authentication from Vault decryption so optional synchronization does not turn the server into a trusted Vault client.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <section><h2>Account password</h2><p>The server receives the Account password over the protected connection and verifies it against a password digest. It identifies the Account for Host sessions and quotas. It cannot decrypt a Vault.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Public-page caching</h2><p>The landing, privacy, security, and glossary pages contain one anonymous representation with no Account data, CSRF token, or session cookie. A shared CDN may cache only those exact successful pages. Signed-in presentation is requested privately and is never shared-cache content.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Search boundary</h2><p>Search materializations are encrypted, rebuildable, local-only, and excluded from synchronization and Vault packages. The optional local model is hash-verified before use and disables network fallback during inference. Remote embedding providers are not part of the current canonical application surface.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Recovery Phrase</h2><p>The 12-word Recovery Phrase remains client-held. A Client uses it to recover local Vault access and enroll a fresh Client Credential. AWSM cannot recover it for you.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Encrypted synchronization</h2><p>A Replica Host stores opaque encrypted items and enforces its own protocol and operational rules. It does not interpret captured titles, page text, screenshots, or Vault keys.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Host Access Grant and future protection</h2><p>Revoking a Host Access Grant prevents future Host operations through that Grant. It cannot erase plaintext or keys already present in a Client installation. Vault authority changes and Key Epoch transitions remain client-held; AWSM does not promise remote wipe.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Backups and portability</h2><p>Synchronization is not a substitute for a Complete Export. Keep a verified Export and the Recovery Phrase in appropriate, separate safe places.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Technical detail</h2><p><%= link_to "Read the current security model", public_product_links[:security_model] %> for the formal trust assumptions and known boundaries.</p></section>
  </div>
</main>
<%= render "shared/public_footer" %>
